{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator attestation for the fourth [operator-attested] criterion: the genuine defect is filed\nas its own ticket and linked discovered_from this one.\n\nThis is tracker state, not repository state, so it cannot be evidenced by a file in the code\nsnapshot. Concrete artifacts, captured 2026-08-12:\n\nTicket identity:\n  rebar show dd41-239d-6e09-4a86\n  -> ticket_id dd41-239d-6e09-4a86, alias rutile-massive-spoonbill, ticket_type bug,\n     status open, tags [completion, llm, regression],\n     title \"Completion verifier false unmet: suppressed governed read is never recovered\"\n\nDurable event evidence on the shared store (git -C .tickets-tracker ls-tree -r --name-only\norigin/tickets | grep dd41-239d-6e09-4a86):\n  dd41-239d-6e09-4a86/1786518284814112001-80ca0372-5799-4ba3-9c6a-76768e218ec0-CREATE.json\n  dd41-239d-6e09-4a86/1786518315091400001-3bc2084a-b3dc-49c0-95ef-bd72a878f6ef-LINK.json\n\nLink direction, which is why it does not appear in this ticket's own deps array: the link was\ncreated as `rebar link rutile-massive-spoonbill shiftable-underage-waterdogs discovered_from`,\nso the outbound dep lives on the CHILD (dd41) and this ticket carries it as an INBOUND dep.\nrebar show shiftable-underage-waterdogs reports:\n  inbound_deps: [{'from_id': 'dd41-239d-6e09-4a86', 'relation': 'discovered_from',\n                  'status': 'open'}]\n  deps:         [{'target_id': '0707-59ae-7db6-489b', 'relation': 'discovered_from', ...}]\nThis is the correct orientation for \"new work discovered from this ticket\" per the AGENTS.md\ncreate + link discovered_from convention, and matches this ticket's own discovered_from link to\n0707-59ae-7db6-489b.\n\nStore synchronization at the time of attestation:\n  git -C .tickets-tracker rev-list --left-right --count origin/tickets...HEAD -> 0  0\n  git -C .tickets-tracker rev-parse origin/tickets -> 29cbaef96ef36ecb9d2829e42e1a7f120c26466a\nso both the CREATE and the LINK are present on the shared origin/tickets store, not only\nlocally.\n\nNote for the record: an earlier close attempt reported show_ticket('dd41-239d-6e09-4a86') as\n'Ticket not found' even though both events were already present on origin/tickets. The gate's\nmaterialized ticket snapshot appears to lag newly created sibling tickets. That is a gate\nobservation only; it does not affect this ticket's disposition, and dd41 is verifiable by the\ncommands above.\n\ndd41 is deliberately left OPEN and unimplemented: its indicated fix (re-execute or carry\nforward a suppressed governed call) is a behavior change to completion run budgeting and needs\noperator approval before implementation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786519031943809001,"uuid":"a1a1bd79-8189-49bd-af32-825287accca7"}